n{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}, y = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x + β_{2}x^{2} + β_{3}x^{3}$ that best fits the data.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1^{2} & 1^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2^{2} & 2^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3^{2} & 3^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4^{2} & 4^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & 5^{2} & 5^{3}\\end{bmatrix}, β = \\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}, y = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186134109 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $9$ | $0$ | $-9$ | $-12$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y = β_{0} + β_{2}x^{2} + β_{3}x^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix} = (X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y$,\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" "| $x$ | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $9$ | $0$ | $-9$ | $-12$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y = β_{0} + β_{2}x^{2} + β_{3}x^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix} = (X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?"] [:db/cas 17592186134113 :question/problem "| $x_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x_{2}$ | **$10$** | **$12$** | **$15$** | **$18$** | **$22$** |\n| $x_{3}$ | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$3$** | **$7$** | **$12$** |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the hyperplane $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x_{1} + β_{2}x_{2} + β_{3}x_{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix} = (X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y$,\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" "| $x_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x_{2}$ | **$10$** | **$12$** | **$15$** | **$18$** | **$22$** |\n| $x_{3}$ | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$3$** | **$7$** | **$12$** |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the hyperplane $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x_{1} + β_{2}x_{2} + β_{3}x_{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix} = (X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?"] [:db/cas 17592186134126 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)2xdV$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n$R = {(x, y, z): (x, z) ∈ D, 0 \\le y \\le z}$,\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x = 1$, and the line $z = 2x$ in the first quadrant." "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle ∭_(R)2xdV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n$R = {(x, y, z): (x, z) ∈ D, 0 \\le y \\le z}$,\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x = 1$, and the line $z = 2x$ in the first quadrant."] [